 status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NITTA YOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMAMURA HARUNARI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO, KAZUYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOSHINA, HIZURU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NITTA, YOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMAMURA, HARUNARI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO KAZUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOSHINA HIZURU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NITTA YOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMAMURA HARUNARI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO, KAZUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOSHINA, HIZURU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NITTA, YOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMAMURA, HARUNARI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A non-aqueous electrolyte secondary cell is characterized in that the negative plate is made chiefly of composite particles of which at least part of the core particles containing at least one kind among tin, silicon, and zinc as a constituent element are coated with a solid solution or an intermetallic compound consisting of the constituent element constituting the core particles and at least one element selected from the group consisting of Group 2 elements of the periodic table except the constituent element, transition elements, Group 12 elements, Group 13 elements, and Group 14 elements except carbon and in that the non-aqueous electrolyte is prepared by dissolving an organic acid anion lithium salt into a highly non-oxidizable organic solvent.  Therefore, gas is hardly produced even while the secondary cell is stored at high temperatures, and the secondary cell has a high energy density, excellent cycle life characteristics, and excellent high-rate charging/discharging characteristics.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une cellule secondaire d'un électrolyte non aqueux. Cette cellule se caractérise en ce que la plaque négative se compose essentiellement de particules composites dont au moins une partie des particules centrales contiennent au moins un élément parmi de l'étain, du silicium, et du zinc comme constituant principal. En outre, ces particules sont recouvertes d'une solution solide ou d'un composé intermétallique se composant de l'élément constituant des particules centrales et d'au moins un élément sélectionné dans le groupe se composant d'éléments du groupe 2 du tableau périodique, à l'exception de l'élément constituant, d'éléments de transition, d'éléments du groupe 12, d'éléments du groupe 13, et d'éléments du groupe 14 à l'exception du carbone. L'électrolyte non aqueux est préparé en dissolvant le sel de lithium d'anion acide organique dans un solvant organique fortement non oxydable. Par conséquent, la quantité de gaz produite est pratiquement négligeable même lorsque la cellule secondaire est conservée à des températures élevées. La cellule secondaire présente une forte densité d'énergie, d'excellentes caractéristiques de durée de vie et d'excellentes caractéristiques de chargement/déchargement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>